# kermanych/.env — copy to `.env` and fill in. The real .env is gitignored.
#
# These two are needed ONLY to run GitHub sign-in against a LOCAL Supabase stack:
# `supabase/config.toml` substitutes them into [auth.external.github] via env(),
# so they must exist in the shell (or in this file) BEFORE `supabase start`.
#
# The HOSTED project does not read this file at all — it keeps the same pair in
# the Supabase dashboard under Authentication → Providers → GitHub. So a teammate
# working against the hosted project never needs either value.
#
# For local work, create your OWN throwaway GitHub OAuth App
# (https://github.com/settings/developers) with callback URL
# http://127.0.0.1:54421/auth/v1/callback. Nobody has to share theirs.
#
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID is public; GITHUB_SECRET is the only real secret in this repo.
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=Ov23liXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
GITHUB_SECRET=replace-with-your-own-oauth-app-secret
